Monday remembers Sunday — the week-boundary continuity fix, 18 Sept.

Ali, from the unit: "lack of continuity for peopl on a pod over the weekend but differnet one
on monday - its difficult as treated by week at present."

THE FIRST DIAGNOSIS WAS WRONG. The obvious candidate was the Saturday-pod hold in autoFillDay
(-3000, ratified 29 Jul) stopping at Sunday — but autoFillDay is the FALLBACK path. Since
26.08.20 the live writer is Planner.writeWeek.

THE REAL CAUSE was one line and its absence. rollHistory has always finished every week with
`hist.home = week.home || hist.home` and NOTHING HAS EVER READ IT. Home pods were chosen from
scratch every week, so `offHome` — the cost that keeps a person in one place — meant nothing
across the boundary. Monday had no memory of Sunday by construction, not by a missing rule.

Seeding `home` from it directly was tried first and BROKE RATIFIED RULE 5: a carried person
claimed their pod before the long-day and airway sort ran, taking a slot a long day needed.
So the carry is scored instead, at 14 — beneath the long-day term (40) and the airway term
(20), where it can tip a choice between equal pods and never take a pod the day needs.

Measured on the real 13-week Optima roster (tests/monday-hold-sim.js, new):
  Sunday→Monday same pod    14.3%  ->  38.1%
  Pods per person per week  1.156  ->  1.137
  Pod E with no long day        6  ->      5
  Within-week same pod      92.1%  ->  91.2%   (the only cost)

Tests: planner suite (gold standard, matched pair) ALL 1413 PASS · rule 133 passed / 1 failed,
identical to pristine in an in-place A/B (pre-existing "Pod E biggest 22 days 6.0%") ·
render 303/1 pre-existing · strength 135/0 · locum probe 27/0.

NOTE FOR THE NEXT SESSION: the deployed planner.js and the copy the gold-standard suite tests
against (docs/CCU Pod Allocator/resident/planner.js) had DRIFTED — the deployed one carries
airwayLDPairGap (26.08.25) and the tested one did not, so the suite has never been run against
what is actually live. Both copies carry this change; the drift itself still needs closing.
